I now have a complete and verified understanding. Let me confirm my analysis of the full `.text` layout:

- **0x4003d0** `_start` → calls `__libc_start_main(0x400507, ...)` → **main = 0x400507**
- **0x400400, 0x400410, 0x400440, 0x400480, 0x4004b0** → CRT/gmon startup artifacts (no-op stubs, `frame_dummy` guard, jump thunks) — **not** part of the user program
- **0x4004b6** → the string-copy helper (called by main at 0x40055a)
- **0x400507** → `main`

So the reachable user program = **{main, helper}**. Format strings confirmed at 0x4012e8 (`Nome troppo lungo: %zu caratteri\n`) and 0x401310 (`Registrato: %s (%zu caratteri)\n`).

Note the off-by-one in the helper: `malloc(0x10)` (16 bytes) but `strcpy` when `len <= 0x16` (copies up to 17 bytes) — I will reproduce this faithfully, not fix it.

Let me write the reconstructed source.


  ────────────────────────────────────────
  ▸ write
    path /tmp/re_task_pahtp3qu/out.c
    content: #include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>

/* FUN_004004b6
 * Allocates a 0x10 (16) byte buffer and copies the name string into it.
 * Returns the allocated pointer if strlen(name) <= 0x10, otherwise NULL.
 */
static char *copia_nome(char *name)
{
    size_t len;
    char *dest;

    len = strlen(name);
    if (len <= 0x10) {
        dest = (char *)malloc(0x10);
        strcpy(dest, name);
    }
    else {
        dest = (char *)0;
    }
    return dest;
}

/* FUN_00400507 */
int main(int argc, char **argv)
{
    int i;
    char *s;
    size_t len;

    setvbuf(stdout, (char *)0, 2, 0);
    for (i = 1; i < argc; i = i + 1) {
        s = copia_nome(argv[i]);
        if (s == (char *)0) {
            len = strlen(argv[i]);
            printf("Nome troppo lungo: %zu caratteri\n", len);
        }
        else {
            len = strlen(s);
            printf("Registrato: %s (%zu caratteri)\n", s, len);
            free(s);
        }
    }
    return 0;
}


